    {
      "id": "claim_a5ea6993a6354870afdcb7bb5f3ad369",
      "statement": "rta-builder compiles the rta CLI from the nested components/trusted-actions Go module using go.mod/go.sum caching (go mod download before copying application source), a GOARCH==TARGETARCH assertion, and a go build invoked with -mod=readonly -trimpath and -ldflags that strip symbols (-s -w) and inject Version (from the component's VERSION file), Commit (RTA_COMMIT build arg), and BuildDate (RTA_BUILD_DATE build arg) via -X; only the static /out/rta binary is copied into the final stage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Containerfile#L354-L383",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8fbf5746b28b15452116aaf9d2bcd5d1f4e3750bf99d83ace4973cddf214cf88:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d2f0ad781438481687f5126ac36bf4d9",
      "statement": "The root Makefile's build-amd64/build-arm64 targets supply RTA_COMMIT as `git rev-parse HEAD` (with a -dirty suffix for an unclean checkout) and RTA_BUILD_DATE as that commit's author timestamp as --build-arg values passed to podman build; the Containerfile excludes .git from the build context, relying on these build args (or Konflux-supplied equivalents) for version provenance instead.",
